>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_function_display`

``` hol4
Refute.register_function_display : unit -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Restores or refreshes Refute's built-in function-witness display
postprocessor.

The built-in registration deduplicates a raw `UPDATE` chain at every
function type `:'a -> 'b`: a witness can carry a point shadowed by a
later, higher-priority one (a model-finder point rendered from an
unrepresented atom, or an independently sampled QC point), and this
postprocessor keeps only the first (highest-priority) occurrence of
each point, leaving the base and every surviving point unchanged.  A
point carrying a display marker (`?`, `_`, or `...`) is never treated
as a duplicate of another, even an alpha-equivalent one: a marker
stands for an unspecified value, so two occurrences are never known to
be the same point.

It is display-only, applied through the same walk
`Refute.register_term_postprocessor` installs into.  A
`register_term_postprocessor` registration at exactly `:'a -> 'b`
replaces this built-in, since registration matches on the pattern; this
idempotent entry point restores it afterward.  It is installed when
`Refute` is loaded and creates no HOL objects.

### See also

[`Refute.register_fmap_display`](#Refute.register_fmap_display),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model reconstruction is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
